data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"check-inputs reports all inputs present, nothing missing. So \"missing\" should be an empty array.\n\nNow write /tmp/readback.json with exactly this JSON on a single line:\n- member: \"qa\"\n- role: \"agent\"\n- branch: \"cs-sandbox/<QA:1>.<GROUP:1>\" (from member.json)\n- missing: [] (empty, since check-inputs reported nothing absent)\n- goal: one sentence in my own words: verify the developer's delivered application against the orchestrator's DESIGN.md in my own clone.\n- scope: one sentence: what I own (verifying the work, reporting) and must not touch (don't fix the app, don't fetch/push, don't hunt elsewhere for work).\n- obligations: one sentence: reply to dispatches, commit work to my branch, write durable results to output dir; machine destroyed at end.\n\nNote: /tmp — the instructions say to use /tmp/opencode for temporary work outside the workspace. But the dispatch explicitly says \"e.g. /tmp/readback.json\". The dispatch is authoritative here, it explicitly suggests /tmp/readback.json. I'll follow the dispatch.\n\nLet me write the file."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793341896,"id":"chatcmpl-2b4794c9","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

